window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_main-3c477c9db409a127"]={"key":"ny_main-3c477c9db409a127","group":"ny_main","uid":"3c477c9db409a127","rank":97,"title":"duncastle yewbank financing decision memorandum","occupation":"financial_investment_analysts","archetype":"authored_doc","subbatch":"corpus_main","prompt":"You are a Financial and Investment Analyst supporting Duncastle Holdings. By Friday, Solveig Chidozie needs a decision memorandum for Yewbank School District’s senior decision maker, who will decide whether to accept Duncastle Holdings’ proposed financing arrangement or retain the current provider. The decision concerns a business-unit financing arrangement serving activity in England and Scotland, and the evidence available to you is the attached `yewbank_stakeholder_evidence_pack.docx`, containing stakeholder emails, interview notes, and feedback. The approval meeting is fixed, but the full jurisdiction-by-jurisdiction review cannot be completed before it, so the senior reader needs a useful, time-bounded comparison without false certainty about matters that remain open. The lowest-cost alternative also conflicts with preserving equivalent termination protection in an edge case, and both cost and protection matter to Yewbank. Prepare one presentation-ready decision memorandum comparing the two alternatives, showing the evidence-supported trade-off, the fallback used for the unresolved position, and the implications of each choice for the senior decision maker. Make clear which statements are firm commitments, which are informal stakeholder views, and which jurisdictional points remain unresolved; do not turn an incomplete review into a claim of compliance. This is decision support, not an instruction to Yewbank: present the facts and implications without recommending or taking the decision, and do not invent figures or legal conclusions that the evidence does not support. Keep the file to no more than seven slides so it can be used in the approval meeting, use clear source attribution, and make the cost comparison and the edge case agree wherever they recur. Write the deliverable as `yewbank_financing_decision_memorandum.pptx` into the top level of the working directory you start in, using exactly that filename, and do not create any additional deliverable.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/yewbank_stakeholder_evidence_pack.docx` — The sole evidence pack for the memorandum: written financing terms, current-provider terms, stakeholder emails, interview notes, and England/Scotland comparison feedback.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `yewbank_financing_decision_memorandum.pptx` — A presentation-ready decision memorandum for Yewbank School District’s senior decision maker comparing Duncastle Holdings’ proposed financing arrangement with retention of the current provider. (Use exactly this filename and write it at the top level of the working directory.; Contain no more than seven slides.; Present facts, evidence status, quantified implications, trade-offs, and the fallback position without making a recommendation or taking the decision.; Use only figures and conclusions supported by the supplied evidence pack, with assumptions and source attribution visible enough for executive review.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/yewbank_stakeholder_evidence_pack.docx","bytes":41022,"extension":".docx","url":"assets/aa717477b1c111aa845ce06f0bf1ba9bdfa366514ae79f6690d568e2caea8223.docx","sha256":"aa717477b1c111aa845ce06f0bf1ba9bdfa366514ae79f6690d568e2caea8223","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"Yewbank School District\nFinancing stakeholder evidence pack\nCommercial extracts, stakeholder communications and review notes assembled for Friday approval preparation. Each item retains its own evidence status; this pack does not resolve the decision.\nSOURCE A | WRITTEN PROPOSED TERMS\nDuncastle Holdings - Indicative Financing Term Sheet (v1.3)\nEvidence status: Documented proposed commercial terms only. Subject to final documentation, approvals and execution; not an executed unconditional commitment.\n\nFacility amount\n£8,000,000\nTerm and repayment\nFive years; interest-only. The £8,000,000 principal remains outstanding during this comparison horizon.\nFixed annual interest rate\n4.80% p.a.\nArrangement fee\n0.75% of principal (£60,000), payable at inception.\nEarly termination\nExit in year three: 3% of outstanding principal (£240,000 while £8,000,000 remains outstanding).\nProvider-failure exception\nNone in the written terms. No signed exception removes the early-termination fee for this edge case.\n\nSource A: Duncastle Holdings, Indicative Financing Term Sheet v1.3, commercial team circulation.\n\n\nSOURCE B | WRITTEN EXISTING ARRANGEMENT\nCurrent Provider - Existing Arrangement Extract\nEvidence status: Existing documented provider arrangement. The arrangement is available to remain in place through the Friday approval meeting.\n\nFacility amount\n£8,000,000\nComparison basis\nSame five-year interest-only basis; principal remains outstanding for the comparison.\nFixed annual interest rate\n5.25% p.a.\nUpfront arrangement fee\nNone.\nTermination\nYewbank may terminate on 90 days' written notice without an early-termination charge.\nAvailability\nExisting arrangement can remain in place through Friday's approval meeting.\n\nSource B: Current Provider, Existing Arrangement Extract, facility operations record.\n\n\nSOURCE C | INFORMAL STAKEHOLDER VIEW\nEmail - Milena Fournier\nFrom\nMilena Fournier\nTo\nSolveig Chidozie\nSubject\nDuncastle exit fee\nStatus\nInformal stakeholder view; no contractual amendment attached\n\nAfter a quick call, I understand Duncastle may be able to waive the early-termination fee where a provider failure drives the exit, but this would need internal approval. Nothing in writing has been issued and I do not have confirmation that a waiver has been approved. Please do not treat the waiver as agreed until an approved written exception is available.\nSource C: Email from Milena Fournier, subject 'Duncastle exit fee'.\nSOURCE E | YEWBANK STAKEHOLDER FEEDBACK\nFeedback - Jacinta Zieliński\nFrom\nJacinta Zieliński\nTo\nSolveig Chidozie\nSubject\nTermination protection\nStatus\nYewbank stakeholder requirement and concern\n\nEquivalent termination protection must be preserved in the provider-failure or early-exit edge case. The lower financing cost matters to Yewbank, but the protection requirement is not to be silently traded away.\nSource E: Feedback from Jacinta Zieliński, subject 'Termination protection'.\n\n\nSOURCE D | INTERNAL REVIEW NOTES\nInterview notes - Ragnhild Novotny\nEvidence status: Internal review evidence and professional interpretation, with explicit jurisdictional status boundaries.\n\nEngland review\nComplete. The internal equivalence criterion is no-fee termination on material provider failure with stated notice protection.\nEngland mapping\nThe Current Provider's documented protection - no-fee termination on 90 days' notice - maps to the completed England criterion.\nScotland review\nThe Scotland review and jurisdictional mapping are incomplete before the Friday approval meeting.\nScotland boundary\nThe incomplete Scotland review supports no conclusion that either alternative is compliant or equivalent there. The England conclusion does not close the Scotland question.\n\nSource D: Ragnhild Novotny interview notes, jurisdiction comparison review.\nSOURCE F | OPERATIONAL FEASIBILITY\nOperational feedback - Lars Underwood\nFrom\nLars Underwood\nTo\nSolveig Chidozie\nSubject\nFriday continuity\nStatus\nOperational feasibility observation\n\nRetaining the Current Provider is operationally available through Friday and can serve as a temporary fallback while documented Duncastle protection and the Scotland jurisdiction review remain unresolved.\nSource F: Operational feedback from Lars Underwood, subject 'Friday continuity'.","truncated":false,"note":"DOCX 正文与表格单元格文字提取；不还原分页、字体与版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/yewbank_financing_decision_memorandum.pptx","bytes":46203,"extension":".pptx","url":"assets/8637f5a727bf14609bc251334df0cd97a72e3f6c8d2182393a4020e228da4b6b.pptx","sha256":"8637f5a727bf14609bc251334df0cd97a72e3f6c8d2182393a4020e228da4b6b","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"=== 幻灯片 1 ===\nDECISION MEMORANDUM\nYewbank financing decision memorandum\nFor Yewbank School District's senior decision maker | Friday approval meeting\nDecision: accept Duncastle Holdings' proposed financing arrangement or retain the Current Provider.\nThe record creates a real trade-off: lower five-year financing cost versus equivalent termination protection, with Scotland still unresolved.\n£120,000\nlower five-year baseline cash cost under Duncastle\n£192,000\nhigher Duncastle cash cost in the documented year-three early-exit case\nOPEN\nScotland review and jurisdictional mapping remain incomplete by Friday\nDecision boundary: written terms, informal stakeholder views, and unresolved review findings are not interchangeable evidence.\nThis memorandum presents facts and implications; decision authority remains with Yewbank.\nSources: Evidence pack A-F | Written terms, stakeholder communications, review notes and operational feedback\n1 / 7\n\n=== 幻灯片 2 ===\nEVIDENCE BASE\nCommercial terms and evidence status\nThe written alternatives are distinct; the possible waiver remains an informal, unconfirmed view.\nDOCUMENTED PROPOSAL\nDuncastle Holdings\nIndicative Financing Term Sheet v1.3\n£8,000,000 | 5 years | interest-only\n- Fixed annual rate: 4.80%\n- Upfront arrangement fee: 0.75% (£60,000)\n- Year-three exit: 3.00% of outstanding principal (£240,000)\n- No signed provider-failure exception in written terms\nStatus: proposed terms only; subject to final documentation, approvals and execution. Not an unconditional commitment.\nDOCUMENTED EXISTING ARRANGEMENT\nCurrent Provider\nExisting Arrangement Extract\n£8,000,000 | same 5-year interest-only comparison\n- Fixed annual rate: 5.25%\n- Upfront arrangement fee: none\n- Termination: 90 days' written notice; no early-termination charge\n- Existing arrangement can remain in place through Friday\nStatus: written existing arrangement. These are the available incumbent terms, not an informal preference.\nINFORMAL / UNCONFIRMED | Milena: Duncastle may waive the fee after internal approval.\nNo written amendment or approved exception; excluded from the quantified base case.\nSources: A Duncastle Holdings, Indicative Financing Term Sheet v1.3 | B Current Provider, Existing Arrangement Extract | C Milena Fournier email\n2 / 7\n\n=== 幻灯片 3 ===\nFINANCIAL COMPARISON\nFive-year baseline cash cost: Duncastle is lower by £120,000\nA transparent interest-only comparison on the same unchanged principal; this is not an assumed waiver outcome.\nDUNCASTLE\n£1.980m\nFive-year baseline financing cash cost\n£1,920,000 interest (£8,000,000 x 4.80% x 5)\n+£60,000 upfront fee\nIncludes the written one-time arrangement fee. Principal repayment is not included because the same principal remains outstanding for both alternatives.\nCURRENT PROVIDER\n£2.100m\nFive-year baseline financing cash cost\n£2,100,000 interest (£8,000,000 x 5.25% x 5)\n£0 upfront fee\nNo upfront arrangement fee is added. The comparison uses the same interest-only and unchanged-principal treatment as Duncastle.\nMODEL ASSUMPTIONS\n5-year horizon | interest-only | £8,000,000 principal unchanged and outstanding | principal repayment excluded as common | Duncastle £60,000 fee included once | Current Provider fee £0\nSources: A Duncastle Holdings, Indicative Financing Term Sheet v1.3 | B Current Provider, Existing Arrangement Extract | calculations shown\n3 / 7\n\n=== 幻灯片 4 ===\nEDGE CASE\nYear-three early-exit case: the cost ranking reverses\nExit after 3 years of interest-only payments; £8,000,000 principal is still outstanding.\nDUNCASTLE\n£1.452m\nYear-three early-exit cash cost\n£1,152,000 interest + £60,000 upfront fee\n+£240,000 early-termination charge (3.00% of £8,000,000)\nThe documented fee is used; no waiver is assumed.\nCURRENT PROVIDER\n£1.260m\nYear-three early-exit cash cost\n£1,260,000 interest + £0 upfront fee\n£0 early-termination charge\nWritten termination right: 90 days' notice without a charge.\nDuncastle is £192,000 more expensive than the Current Provider in this year-three edge case.\nThe cheapest five-year baseline option is not unconditionally superior: its documented termination fee reverses the result in the edge case.\nMilena's possible waiver is informal, subject to internal approval and not documented; it is not included in either quantified case.\nSources: A Duncastle Holdings, Indicative Financing Term Sheet v1.3 | B Current Provider, Existing Arrangement Extract | C Milena Fournier email\n4 / 7\n\n=== 幻灯片 5 ===\nPROTECTION AND REVIEW BOUNDARY\nTermination protection and jurisdiction status\nEngland is a completed internal comparison; Scotland remains an explicit evidence boundary at the approval meeting.\nYEWBANK REQUIREMENT | Equivalent termination protection must be preserved in the provider-failure / early-exit edge case.\nENGLAND | COMPLETE\nCompleted internal equivalence review\nCriterion: no-fee termination on material provider failure with stated notice protection.\nCurrent Provider: documented no-fee termination on 90 days' notice maps to the completed England criterion.\nDuncastle: written term sheet carries a 3.00% early-termination fee; no signed provider-failure exception is documented.\nEngland status is limited to this completed internal comparison.\nSCOTLAND | INCOMPLETE\nReview and jurisdictional mapping\nopen\nThe Scotland review is incomplete as of the Friday approval meeting.\nNo definitive compliance or equivalence conclusion for either alternative. England's completed result does not close the Scotland question.\nThis is an unresolved review item, not proof that either alternative complies with or satisfies a Scotland requirement.\nStatus reflects review progress, not a legal signoff.\nSources: D Ragnhild Novotny interview notes | E Jacinta Zieliński feedback | A/B written financing terms\n5 / 7\n\n=== 幻灯片 6 ===\nDECISION IMPLICATIONS\nImplications of each choice at Friday\nBoth choices retain the unresolved Scotland limitation; neither is presented as risk-free or cost-free.\nDUNCASTLE PROPOSED FINANCING\nCommercial implication\n- £120,000 lower five-year baseline financing cost\n- Written 3.00% fee makes the year-three edge case £192,000 higher than the Current Provider\n- No documented provider-failure protection amendment; possible waiver remains informal and unconfirmed\n- Scotland mapping is incomplete; no equivalence or compliance conclusion is drawn\nRETAIN CURRENT PROVIDER\nCommercial and continuity implication\n- £120,000 higher five-year baseline financing cost\n- Documented 90-day notice and no-fee termination; maps to completed England criterion\n- Available through Friday, providing continuity and temporary fallback value\n- Scotland mapping remains incomplete; this is not a settled Scotland conclusion\nThe lower baseline cost and equivalent termination protection collide in the documented early-exit case.\nSources: A/B written terms | C Milena Fournier email | D Ragnhild Novotny interview notes | E Jacinta Zieliński feedback | F Lars Underwood feedback\n6 / 7\n\n=== 幻灯片 7 ===\nCLOSING DECISION BOUNDARY\nDecision implications and time-bounded fallback\nDecision owner: Yewbank School District's senior decision maker.\nDUNCASTLE\nLower baseline, open protection position\n£120,000 lower over five years, but the written provider-failure / early-exit protection change is not documented and Scotland remains open.\nCURRENT PROVIDER\nHigher baseline, documented continuity\n£120,000 higher over five years, with written 90-day no-fee termination / England mapping and continuity through Friday; Scotland remains open.\nTEMPORARY FALLBACK / HOLD\nIf a documented Duncastle protection amendment and a completed Scotland review are not available by Friday, retention of the Current Provider is the time-bounded fallback through the approval meeting.\nThis memorandum informs the decision; it does not assign or take the decision for Yewbank.\nSources: A/B written terms | D Ragnhild Novotny interview notes | F Lars Underwood feedback | calculations shown on Slides 3-4\n7 / 7","truncated":false,"note":"PPTX 共7页的文字提取；不还原位置、动画和版式。","embedded_image_count":0,"embedded_images":[]}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The submitted artifact is a PowerPoint file with the exact required filename.","weight":1.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted file name and MIME/package structure.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the top-level submitted file is named yewbank_financing_decision_memorandum.pptx and is a valid OOXML presentation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"file_introspection","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation opens successfully and contains readable slide content rather than a corrupt or empty package.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered slides and extracted presentation text.","grader_hint":"Open or render the PPTX and verify that the slides load, contain substantive content, and do not show package or rendering errors."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"geometry","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum contains no more than seven slides.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":true,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Slide count in the submitted PPTX.","grader_hint":"Count the slides in the presentation package; seven is the maximum."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The presentation is usable in an executive approval meeting: its text is legible, the alternatives and central tension are easy to locate, and charts or tables do not obscure the underlying comparison.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered presentation as a whole.","grader_hint":"Review the rendered slides at normal presentation scale for legibility, hierarchy, unclipped text, coherent visual comparison, and absence of distracting or decorative material that displaces the decision content."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies Yewbank School District’s senior decision maker as the audience and states that the decision is whether to accept Duncastle Holdings’ proposed financing or retain the current provider.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Decision framing and audience statement in the memorandum.","grader_hint":"Find an explicit decision frame naming Yewbank, Duncastle, the current provider, and the senior decision-maker audience."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The comparison treats Duncastle’s proposal and retention of the current provider as two distinct alternatives throughout the memorandum, rather than comparing one option against an unnamed baseline.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Alternative labels in the comparison, cost model, and implications.","grader_hint":"Check that the same two alternatives recur consistently in the decision frame, financial comparison, protection comparison, and implications."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum accurately records the principal, term, interest rate, upfront fee, and early-termination-fee terms for Duncastle and the corresponding principal, term, rate, fee, and notice terms for the current provider, as stated in the evidence pack.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Financial terms table or equivalent comparison, checked against the written source items.","grader_hint":"Compare every commercial input against the Duncastle term sheet and current-provider extract in the supplied pack; allow no silent substitution of a rate, term, fee, or notice condition."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The five-year baseline cash cost shown for Duncastle is £1,980,000 ±£1.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Baseline cost model and displayed total.","grader_hint":"Verify the total using five years of interest-only cost on the supplied principal at the Duncastle fixed rate plus the supplied upfront arrangement fee."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The five-year baseline cash cost shown for the current provider is £2,100,000 ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Baseline cost model and displayed total.","grader_hint":"Verify the total using five years of interest-only cost on the supplied principal at the current-provider rate and the supplied absence of an upfront fee."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The baseline cost difference is shown as £120,000 ±£1 in Duncastle’s favour, with the direction of the comparison stated correctly.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Savings or difference calculation in the financial comparison.","grader_hint":"Recalculate current-provider baseline cost minus Duncastle baseline cost and check both the amount and whether it is described as a saving or premium."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The financial comparison states the assumptions needed to interpret the totals, including the interest-only treatment, unchanged principal, five-year horizon, and treatment of the upfront fee.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Model assumptions or explanatory note adjacent to the cost comparison.","grader_hint":"Confirm that a reader can reproduce the baseline totals without guessing whether principal amortizes, whether the fee is included, or what time horizon is being used."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For the documented year-three early-exit edge case, the Duncastle cash cost is shown as £1,452,000 ±£1.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Edge-case calculation in the memorandum.","grader_hint":"Verify three years of Duncastle interest, the upfront fee, and the 3% early-termination charge on the still-outstanding £8,000,000 principal."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For the same year-three early-exit edge case, the current-provider cash cost is shown as £1,260,000 ±£1.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Matched edge-case calculation for the current provider.","grader_hint":"Verify three years of current-provider interest with no early-termination charge or upfront fee, using the same principal and timing assumptions as the Duncastle case."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"value_tolerance","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum shows that Duncastle is £192,000 ±£1 more expensive than the current provider in the year-three edge case.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Edge-case difference or comparison statement.","grader_hint":"Recalculate Duncastle edge-case cost minus current-provider edge-case cost and check the direction as well as the amount."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum explicitly distinguishes the lower five-year baseline cost from the adverse year-three edge-case result and states that the cheapest baseline option is not unconditionally superior.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Synthesis around the cost table and trade-off statement.","grader_hint":"Look for a direct comparison of the two scenarios, not merely two disconnected tables whose implication must be inferred."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Duncastle commercial terms are attributed to the written term sheet as documented proposed terms, without presenting the proposal as a final unconditional commitment.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source note, footnote, or evidence-status label attached to Duncastle terms.","grader_hint":"Check that the memorandum identifies the term sheet and preserves its proposed or conditional status rather than upgrading it to an executed guarantee."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The current-provider rate and termination terms are attributed to the written current-provider material and are treated as the available existing arrangement rather than as informal stakeholder preference.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Source attribution beside the incumbent alternative.","grader_hint":"Confirm that the current-provider terms trace to the written provider material in the evidence pack."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies the suggestion that Duncastle might waive the termination fee as informal or unconfirmed and does not include it in the quantified base case.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Treatment of Milena’s stakeholder communication and the financial model.","grader_hint":"Find an explicit qualification such as informal, verbal, subject to approval, or not documented, and verify that the waiver is not silently used to reduce the Duncastle cost."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum states Yewbank’s requirement or concern that equivalent termination protection must be preserved, including in the relevant provider-failure or early-exit edge case.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Requirements or decision-criteria statement.","grader_hint":"Look for the protection requirement in terms stronger than a general preference for flexibility or low cost."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The England comparison correctly records that the review is complete and that the current provider’s documented no-fee termination protection with the stated notice period meets the internal equivalence criterion described in the evidence pack.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"England row or passage in the jurisdiction comparison.","grader_hint":"Check both the England status and the mapped protection; do not award credit for merely naming England."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"substring","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Scotland comparison explicitly says that the review or mapping is incomplete as of the approval meeting and gives no definitive compliance or equivalence conclusion.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Scotland row or limitation statement.","grader_hint":"The wording must preserve the open status; a generic statement that more work is needed is sufficient only if it clearly applies to Scotland and the approval deadline."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum does not describe the incomplete Scotland review as proof that either alternative complies with or satisfies the Scotland requirement.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"All Scotland-related claims across the presentation.","grader_hint":"Inspect the executive summary, comparison table, and conclusion for unsupported words such as compliant, cleared, confirmed, or equivalent when applied to the unresolved Scotland position."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum keeps jurisdictional evidence separate: it does not use the completed England review to close the unresolved Scotland question or collapse both jurisdictions into one status.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Jurisdiction comparison and synthesis.","grader_hint":"Check that England and Scotland have distinct statuses and that any cross-jurisdiction conclusion is explicitly limited."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum identifies retention of the current provider as the fallback or hold position while the Duncastle protection amendment and/or the unresolved Scotland review remain open.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fallback statement in the decision implications.","grader_hint":"Award credit only if the fallback is explicit and tied to the current-provider alternative, rather than being an unlabelled suggestion to delay."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The fallback is time-bounded and conditional: it is connected to the Friday approval meeting and to the absence of a documented Duncastle protection change or completed Scotland review, rather than being presented as a permanent conclusion.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Fallback condition and timing language.","grader_hint":"Look for both the deadline and the unresolved conditions; a bare statement to retain the current provider is not enough."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The Duncastle implications include the quantified baseline saving together with the termination-protection exposure and unresolved Scotland status.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Duncastle alternative implications.","grader_hint":"Verify that the Duncastle case is not described only as a price opportunity and that the cost and protection consequences are linked."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The current-provider implications include the higher quantified baseline cost together with the documented no-fee termination protection, continuity/fallback value, and the limitation that Scotland review remains open.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Current-provider alternative implications.","grader_hint":"Check for a balanced treatment of the incumbent rather than a portrayal as risk-free or cost-free."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum remains decision support and does not recommend, direct, or rank one alternative as the analyst’s decision.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Executive summary, option implications, and closing slide.","grader_hint":"A balanced statement of implications is acceptable; phrases such as recommend, choose Duncastle, approve, reject, or should retain must not assign the decision to the analyst."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"All displayed financial figures and jurisdictional conclusions are traceable to the evidence pack or to transparent calculations from its figures; no unsupported rate, fee, legal threshold, or compliance status is introduced.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete presentation, source notes, and calculations.","grader_hint":"Reconcile every material number and legal or compliance assertion to a source item or clearly shown arithmetic; do not penalize reasonable rounding when the underlying value is evident."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The memorandum distinguishes documented terms or commitments, stakeholder views, and unresolved review items in a way that prevents a reader from treating all evidence as equally authoritative.","weight":4.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Evidence-status labels and narrative qualifications.","grader_hint":"Review whether source type and status are visible for the term sheet, current-provider material, informal waiver comment, and jurisdiction review notes."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Material claims and figures have usable source attribution to the evidence pack, including enough identification of the relevant email, interview note, feedback item, or written term material for an executive reviewer to trace them.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Footnotes, source tags, or source column in the memorandum.","grader_hint":"Generic attribution to an unnamed source is insufficient for material claims; check that the source labels correspond to items in the supplied pack."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"relational_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Alternative names, cost terminology, jurisdiction labels, and protection terminology remain consistent across the executive frame, tables, and closing implications.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cross-slide terminology audit.","grader_hint":"Check that the same alternative is not renamed or assigned different rates, fees, statuses, or protection descriptions in different parts of the deck."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"A senior decision maker can understand the decision frame, baseline financial result, edge-case reversal, evidence limitations, and fallback without asking the analyst to interpret an unexplained table.","weight":3.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Rendered deck as an executive communication.","grader_hint":"Judge whether the narrative makes the consequence of the trade-off explicit and whether the reader can distinguish known facts from open questions without oral supplementation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"constraint_predicate","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The presentation closes on the decision implications and the bounded unresolved position, not on an analyst-assigned recommendation or an unprioritized list of next steps.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Final slide and final substantive text.","grader_hint":"Inspect the ending of the deck; it should leave the senior decision maker with the two option implications and the conditional fallback, while preserving decision authority."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"This is bounded finance decision support for a school district financing approval, where the analyst must reconcile commercial terms, stakeholder reliability, and incomplete cross-jurisdiction evidence. The memorandum will be read by a senior decision maker under a fixed meeting deadline.","difficulty_sources":["Reconcile written financing terms, existing-provider terms, stakeholder emails, interview notes, and feedback by evidence status.","Model a five-year baseline and a year-three early-exit edge case whose cost ranking reverses.","Synthesize a bounded England comparison with an explicitly unresolved Scotland review.","State a defensible time-bounded fallback without converting decision support into an analyst recommendation.","Maintain consistent figures, terminology, source attribution, and implications across a compact executive presentation."],"authoring_plan":{"source_construction":{"filename":"yewbank_stakeholder_evidence_pack.docx","purpose":"Create one coherent offline evidence pack containing the only facts needed to produce and grade the memorandum.","contents":[{"source_item":"Written Duncastle proposal","reliability":"Documented proposed commercial terms, not an executed unconditional commitment.","facts":["Principal is £8,000,000.","Term is five years and interest-only, leaving the principal outstanding during the comparison horizon.","Fixed annual rate is 4.80%.","Upfront arrangement fee is 0.75% of principal, or £60,000.","If Yewbank exits in year three, the proposed early-termination fee is 3% of the outstanding principal, or £240,000.","The written terms contain no signed exception removing that fee for the provider-failure edge case."]},{"source_item":"Written current-provider terms","reliability":"Existing documented provider arrangement.","facts":["Principal and five-year interest-only comparison basis are the same.","Fixed annual rate is 5.25%.","There is no upfront arrangement fee.","Yewbank may terminate on 90 days’ notice without an early-termination charge.","The existing arrangement can remain in place through the Friday approval meeting."]},{"source_item":"Milena Fournier stakeholder email","reliability":"Informal stakeholder view, not a contractual amendment.","facts":["Milena reports that Duncastle may be able to waive the early-termination fee after internal approval.","No written amendment or approved exception accompanies the statement."]},{"source_item":"Ragnhild Novotny interview notes","reliability":"Internal review evidence and professional interpretation, with explicit status boundaries.","facts":["The England review is complete under the internal equivalence criterion: no-fee termination on material provider failure with the stated notice protection.","The current provider’s documented protection maps to the completed England criterion.","The Scotland review and jurisdictional mapping are incomplete before the approval meeting.","The incomplete Scotland review supports no conclusion that either alternative is compliant or equivalent there."]},{"source_item":"Jacinta Zieliński stakeholder feedback","reliability":"Yewbank requirement and preference communicated by a stakeholder.","facts":["Equivalent termination protection is a required concern for Yewbank in the provider-failure edge case.","Yewbank values the lower financing cost but does not want the protection requirement silently traded away."]},{"source_item":"Lars Underwood operational feedback","reliability":"Operational feasibility observation.","facts":["Retaining the current provider is operationally available through Friday and can serve as a temporary fallback while documented protection and jurisdiction review remain unresolved."]}]},"gold_logic":{"baseline_model":["Duncastle interest is £8,000,000 × 4.80% × 5 = £1,920,000; add £60,000 upfront fee for £1,980,000.","Current-provider interest is £8,000,000 × 5.25% × 5 = £2,100,000; no upfront fee is added.","The Duncastle baseline saving is £2,100,000 − £1,980,000 = £120,000."],"edge_case_model":["Use a year-three early exit after three years of interest-only payments, with the £8,000,000 principal still outstanding.","Duncastle cost is £8,000,000 × 4.80% × 3 + £60,000 + £240,000 = £1,452,000.","Current-provider cost is £8,000,000 × 5.25% × 3 = £1,260,000.","Duncastle is therefore £192,000 more expensive in the edge case."],"expected_synthesis":["The proposal is cheaper on the five-year baseline but reverses in the documented year-three early-exit case because of the early-termination fee.","The protection requirement and the lowest baseline cost are individually reasonable but collide in that edge case.","The informal possibility of a fee waiver must not be included as an achieved term.","England can be described using the completed review and mapped protection; Scotland must remain open.","Retention of the current provider is the evidence-supported fallback or hold position through Friday if a written Duncastle amendment and the outstanding Scotland review are not resolved.","The memorandum must present implications for both alternatives and preserve Yewbank’s senior decision maker as the decision owner, without issuing an analyst recommendation."]},"quality_checks":["Verify that the single DOCX source is internally consistent and contains no conflicting rates, fees, terms, statuses, or stakeholder identities.","Verify that all expected numeric outputs can be derived offline from the source facts.","Verify that the source pack makes the difference between written terms, informal views, and incomplete review status explicit enough for a solver to classify evidence.","Verify that a compliant seven-slide-or-fewer deck can state the decision frame, assumptions, baseline comparison, edge case, jurisdiction statuses, evidence qualifications, fallback, and both option implications without requiring an appendix."]},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"single_artifact","structure":"required_sections"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"yewbank_stakeholder_evidence","filename":"yewbank_stakeholder_evidence_pack.docx","purpose":"The sole evidence pack for the memorandum: written financing terms, current-provider terms, stakeholder emails, interview notes, and England/Scotland comparison feedback.","required":true,"discovery":"Open the supplied DOCX in the working directory before preparing the memorandum."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"financing_decision_memorandum","filename":"yewbank_financing_decision_memorandum.pptx","media_type":"application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.presentationml.presentation","description":"A presentation-ready decision memorandum for Yewbank School District’s senior decision maker comparing Duncastle Holdings’ proposed financing arrangement with retention of the current provider.","required":true,"constraints":["Use exactly this filename and write it at the top level of the working directory.","Contain no more than seven slides.","Present facts, evidence status, quantified implications, trade-offs, and the fallback position without making a recommendation or taking the decision.","Use only figures and conclusions supported by the supplied evidence pack, with assumptions and source attribution visible enough for executive review."],"rendering_required":true}],"work_activity":"make_decisions","work_product":"decision_memo","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"authored_doc@v4","occupation":"financial_investment_analysts","sector":"finance_insurance","task_archetype":"authored_doc","estimated_professional_hours":4.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"A finance-domain reviewer should verify the arithmetic, evidence classification, alternative comparison, and bounded decision framing. A second independent reviewer should inspect the rendered slides for executive usability, cross-slide consistency, and unsupported jurisdictional claims.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The Scotland review is intentionally incomplete and must remain unresolved in the gold; no live legal or regulatory research is required or permitted.","The supplied commercial figures are synthetic internal evidence and should be checked against the evidence pack rather than external market data."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:06:51+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:06:51+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:06:51+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-16T16:06:51+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_main/runs/3c477c9db409a127","declared_deliverables":["yewbank_financing_decision_memorandum.pptx"]};
